## Summary

Two gaps in ground item timers:

- **Drops all use the loot timers.** `HeldInteractions` dropped every item with `constants.lootdrop_duration` (200 ticks) and `ObjRepository.DEFAULT_REVEAL_DELAY` (100), so a dropped item vanished after 2 minutes and untradeables became visible to other players after 1 minute. The wiki's [Drop](https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Drop) page: tradeables appear to others after 60 seconds and disappear 120 seconds later; untradeables disappear after 180 seconds; clue scrolls after 61 minutes. A manual drop now gets:
  - tradeable (the cache's Grand Exchange flag `stockmarket`; noted items use their base item): private for 100 ticks, despawns after 300;
  - untradeable: never public, despawns after 300;
  - clue scrolls, challenge scrolls and the Mimic ([Guide:Clue Juggling](https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Guide:Clue_Juggling): "Dropped clue / challenge scrolls and Mimics despawn in exactly 61 minutes"): never public, despawns after 6100.
  
  `ItemServerType.tradeable` can't be used: it defaults to `true` and reads `true` at runtime even for items the cache marks untradeable (a dropped trowel came out public). `player.lootDropDuration` still overrides the duration, and the drop hooks (wilderness) still apply.
- **OBJ_ADD sent no timers.** Every OBJ_ADD had `timeUntilPublic`, `timeUntilDespawn`, `ownershipType` and `neverBecomesPublic` at 0/false. RuneLite builds its ground item timers from these (`TileItem.getDespawnTime()`/`getVisibleTime()`: Ground Items' despawn timer, the Clue Scroll Juggling plugin), so they showed nothing. `ObjRepository` now stores the reveal and despawn cycles on the `Obj`, and `ZoneUpdateTransformer` sends them:
  - to the receiver while the obj is private: ownership self, both timers counted down to the send tick, `neverBecomesPublic` when it has a despawn but no reveal;
  - at the reveal (others only, as before): ownership other, the remaining despawn time;
  - when re-sent after the reveal: ownership other, also to the original receiver;
  - objs without a duration (map spawns): all 0, as before.
- **Obj copies lost their owner.** `ObjRegistry.singleCopy` (a non-stackable drop with count > 1, split into single objs) and `ZoneUpdateTransformer.copy` (the obj kept on private zone prots) built the copy without `ownerId`, so `isOriginalOwner` was false on them. Both pass `ownerId` now.

