## Screenshots / notes for reviewers

RSProx recordings (rsprox.net) of the official game, rev 225-231, all OBJ_ADD/OBJ_DEL for drops (if_button7 on 149:0): tradeable drops are `reveal=100, despawn=300, ownership=self, neverturnpublic=false` and are deleted 299 ticks after the drop tick (recordings 1621, 91, 1718, 3056); untradeable drops `despawn=300, self, neverturnpublic=true` (73, 1694, 1702, 91); beginner and hard clue drops `despawn=6100, self, true` (91, 1702). A private item re-sent later has both timers counted down (73: `reveal=49, despawn=249`); after the reveal it comes back as `ownership=other` with the remaining despawn time, also to the player who dropped it (73). The owner gets no packet at the reveal. Map spawns send all fields at 0.

Clue items are matched by name ("Clue scroll (tier)", "Challenge scroll (tier)", "Mimic"). The tier categories and tier params also hold the step caskets, and param 623 misses the beginner and master scrolls and the elite challenge scrolls while it matches X Marks the Spot and Song of the Elves quest scrolls.

Not covered here:
- NPC loot: the official server sends `reveal=100, despawn=200` for tradeable loot and never reveals untradeable loot (`neverturnpublic=true`). The packet now reports what the server does, but untradeable NPC loot still turns public after 100 ticks; that's a separate fix.
- Untradeable timers pausing while logged out and following the player across worlds; the 20-hour playtime rule; table items (9 min); random event rewards (3 h).
- A stackable drop merged into an existing private stack resets the stack's timers (existing behaviour, TODO in `ObjRepository`). OBJ_COUNT has no timer field, so the client keeps the first drop's timer.
- `ItemServerType.tradeable` reads true for untradeables (existing, unchanged; death drops and shops read it too).
- OBJ_ADD opflags stay `OpFlags.ALL_SHOWN` (-1); the official server sends 31.

